Executor base through typed LiquidLaneExecutor and ThreeFExecutor entrypoints
├── initialization and caller
│   ├── defaults to no authorized caller
│   ├── only the owner can select the caller or replace configuration
│   ├── rotating or clearing the caller removes old execution permission
│   └── the selected caller needs no adapter leaf roles
├── configuration and permissions
│   ├── stores ordered liquidity sources separately from approval and operation leaves
│   ├── indexed getters and length expose replacement and clearing
│   ├── replacements remove obsolete sources despite their retained Merkle roles
│   ├── supplied liquidity calls match the configured count and order
│   ├── reject changed targets, masks, pinned calldata and native-value class
│   ├── preserve the full 96-bit native value for liquidity calls
│   └── typed operation parameters remain constrained by their configured leaf
├── liquidity preparation
│   ├── spend idle funds above the protected reserve first
│   ├── query each needed source immediately before use
│   ├── require full source capacity unless the remaining need is smaller
│   ├── reject underuse, overuse and balance decreases atomically
│   ├── skip zero-capacity and unnecessary sources
│   └── static queries cannot change state and bubble failures
├── approvals
│   ├── the adapter owns the exact allowance and the executor never holds funding
│   ├── reset existing nonzero allowance before approving the exact amount
│   ├── accept tokens whose approve returns no data
│   ├── reject false or malformed return data and roll back liquidity and allowance
│   └── approval spender, mask, proof and executor role remain constrained
├── adapter authorization
│   ├── executed leaves require current proofs and executor roles
│   ├── caller leaf roles cannot bypass the configured caller restriction
│   ├── skipped liquidity calls need no executor role
│   └── invalid operation proofs roll back earlier funding
├── exact ThreeF principal
│   ├── fund and mint the requested principal through the actual capability
│   ├── smaller live authorization fails the exact funding delta
│   └── larger live authorization fails the capability bound and rolls back funding
└── atomicity
    ├── retain pending allocation and matured deallocation reserves
    ├── revert prior withdrawals when a borrow health floor or asset budget fails
    └── reject reentry and configuration callbacks without retaining effects
